we've had years  of this stuff we you know if anybody was  looking for evidence about  what a terrible human being the  president can be  uh there was plenty there and so um you  know sadly  i i don't know that this is going to  convince anybody new but i think for  folks that we're concerned to begin with  i think this is all the more reason to  get out and vote yeah terry i want to  actually push  push down on one particular scandal and  that's the one over  the president's alleged comments about  fallen soldiers  there have been denials from the white  house and aggressive pushback from the  president  but on the other hand the major players  general mattis general kelly  john allen general dunford they have not  come out and and cleared anything  up doesn't that hurt the president  oh absolutely does especially since  since you know john kelly was the  primary witness  in one of those uh situations so i mean  the fact this  their silence speaks volumes um but  again i go back to the earlier point  this is not changing anybody's  viewpoints if you were offended by this  you were already offended by the fact  that he said four years ago that john  mccain was a loser because he was a  prisoner of war  so look i mean this doesn't change  anybody's view right now sadly or or or  not  you know you if you believe he said it  um you probably believed he said it  you know that he's capable of this kind  of thing it's just it's just not a  a game changer and we're not seeing any  of that yeah robbie let's talk about the  campaigning  itself the president uh has a law and  order message  but in a recent cbs poll more voters  thought that joe biden was trying to  calm things  with protests in cities across america  while the president was trying to incite  violence that's not a good look i would  think if you're campaigning  is joe biden going to get a bump because  of that  well i think that look the president you  know it's the truth the president is the  one going around and citing violence he  was sending federal agents uh  into cities uh that were just making  things much much worse  he wants this he wants this this kind of  upset  um to then try to use it for political  reasons i think people see through that  so i do think joe biden uh is winning on  this right now and  and and the president as with many  things is undermining his own message  you know uh if he really cared about law  and order he would be out there  speaking about coming together uh he  would be doing something about the  problems people are upset about and he's  doing the opposite  yeah terry the president does extremely  well  with white working class voters he did  great with him in 2016.  there's not a lot in the campaign that  seems to be broadening the message in  fact he seems to be trying to go deeper  what do you think of that strategy can  he turn out even more  white working-class voters to lift him  in 2020  well and and yes i think he can do that  and he can also  uh you know suppress the ones that that  don't care about him  all right robbie let's go  do you think the president can turn out  more of those white working-class voters  and will it be enough  yeah i mean this is central to his  strategy if you look at a state like  minnesota for example this is how he  gets it in play  and i think one of the things that terry  maybe was getting to there is i think  for the president it's always two things  turn out more of his base but also  suppress the democratic base  and i think that's a combination of  creating all this confusion about voting  uh you know he's talked about sending  sheriffs out to the polling places to  potentially stop  people coming in but i also do think  you're going to start to see more and  more the president  directing messages at younger voters  particularly younger voters of color  you know with misinformation to try to  get people to stay home because  one of the things we often forget is an  enormous part of the reason hillary lost  four years ago  was people either choosing not to vote  or voting third party for someone else  and he's going to want that same dynamic  this time yeah i think you're going to  see him pull both those levers to try to  do that  yeah there were millions of voters who  voted twice for president obama  and then didn't show up or voted third  party as you point out  let's talk one more uh point of  campaigning here 46 percent of uh  respondents to the recent cbs poll  did not think that biden was campaigning  enough do you expect to see him more  after labor day well they've announced  he's going to be out there more and i  think that was a really good decision  you know the the challenge i i know this  from four years ago the challenge of  running against  donald trump is that he sucks up so much  of the oxygen  voters don't actually hear a lot about  you know his opponent what they want to  do  why they're running what they believe in  and so to do that biden does have to get  out there and i think this was  a good move on their part you know but  i've also you know when you're running  one of these campaigns  uh when you're in that room there's risk  to getting out there more too  and kovid's actually provided you know a  slower  uh pace to the campaign which i think  they've benefited from so  it's a balance but but it's good he's  going to be on the ground and out more  all right robbie milk and terry sullivan  who will be checking on some technical  difficulties there we hope everyone's  okay  thank you to you both of you and we'll  see you again real soon
 

